       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Direct Deposit Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a direct deposit form?\", \"a\": \"It is a short authorization that lets an employer pay wages straight into your bank account. You give the bank name, the nine-digit routing number and your account number, mark checking or savings, and sign. Many employers also ask for a voided check as proof.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make my own direct deposit form?\", \"a\": \"List the fields payroll keys in: the account holder, the bank name, the routing and account numbers, the account type, and a signature with the date. Then decide what proof of the account you accept. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> turns that description into a working form that checks each routing number as it is typed.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you fill out a direct deposit form online?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if your employer offers one in its HR or payroll portal, where you type in your bank details and send them straight to payroll. Some banks also build one from your account online, and Wells Fargo does it in its mobile app and online banking. When your employer has its own version, use that one.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a free direct deposit authorization form?\", \"a\": \"Start with the payroll team at work, since their version matches what their system expects. Failing that, a blank copy of the direct deposit authorization form PDF will do if it carries your name as the bank has it, both numbers, the type of account, and a signature line. An employer that builds its own can start on Emergent for free, with no cap on submissions.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I get a direct deposit form?\", \"a\": \"Ask HR or payroll first. Most employers hand one out with the new-hire paperwork, often on the same portal page as the <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/employee-information-form'>employee information form</a>. If your employer has none, ask your bank whether it can supply one with your numbers already filled in.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do banks give out direct deposit forms?\", \"a\": \"Some do. Wells Fargo, for one, creates a form for whichever account you pick, with both numbers and the checking or savings type already filled in. If your bank offers nothing like it, ask a branch for a letter that lists your routing and account numbers.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do I need a form for direct deposit?\", \"a\": \"Usually, yes. Payroll cannot send wages to your account until it has your bank details and your signed permission for the deposit. Some employers gather those details in an HR portal instead, and that record takes the place of a paper form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does a direct deposit authorization form need a voided check?\", \"a\": \"Not always. Many employers ask for a voided check so payroll can match the printed numbers against the ones you wrote. A letter from your bank proves the same account, and so does a pre-filled form from your bank if it offers one. Either works when you have no checks to void.\"}, {\"q\": \"How long should an employer keep a direct deposit authorization form?\", \"a\": \"Two years after the authorization ends, under the Nacha Operating Rules that govern ACH payments. The clock starts when the employee revokes it, for example by filing a payroll change form for a new account, not when they signed it. With Emergent, each signed authorization lands in a database you own, stamped with its submission date.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is it safe to give someone your direct deposit authorization form?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if it goes to your employer's payroll team through a channel you know, such as the HR portal or a copy you hand over in person. Never send it in reply to an email asking you to switch accounts. The FBI's IC3 has warned that criminals redirect paychecks by changing employees' direct deposit details.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
